parameters.text:
=You are a senior Site Reliability Engineer triaging an incoming monitoring alert.

Alert name: {{ $json.alertName }}
Service: {{ $json.service }}
Reported severity: {{ $json.reportedSeverity }}
Message: {{ $json.alertMessage }}
Metric value: {{ $json.metricValue }} (threshold: {{ $json.threshold }})
Timestamp: {{ $json.alertTimestamp }}

Classify this alert:
- service: the normalized service/system name this alert affects
- alertType: a short category, e.g. 'high_latency', 'error_rate_spike', 'resource_exhaustion', 'deployment_failure', 'infrastructure_drift', 'service_down', or 'other'
- severityAssessed: 'Critical', 'High', 'Medium', or 'Low' based on actual customer/production impact, not just the reported label
- suspectedRootCauseCategory: your best guess at the underlying cause category, e.g. 'bad_deploy', 'resource_saturation', 'dependency_outage', 'config_drift', 'traffic_spike', or 'unknown'
- isCriticalProductionOutage: true if this represents a full or near-full production outage, severe customer-facing impact, or any situation requiring an immediate human page before any automated analysis. When in doubt, set this to true.

Return ONLY a JSON object (no markdown fences, no commentary) with keys: service, alertType, severityAssessed, suspectedRootCauseCategory, isCriticalProductionOutage (boolean), classificationReasoning (one short sentence).

parameters.jsCode:
const upstream = $('Set - Config').first().json;
const response = $input.first().json;

let parsed = {
  service: upstream.service,
  alertType: 'other',
  severityAssessed: 'Critical',
  suspectedRootCauseCategory: 'unknown',
  isCriticalProductionOutage: true,
  classificationReasoning: 'AI classification unavailable this cycle; defaulted to a critical, page-first response.'
};
try {
  const raw = String(response.output || response.text || response.response || '{}').replace(/```json|```/g, '').trim();
  const result = JSON.parse(raw);
  parsed = { ...parsed, ...result };
} catch (e) {
  // keep safe default above
}

return [{
  json: {
    ...upstream,
    service: parsed.service,
    alertType: parsed.alertType,
    severityAssessed: parsed.severityAssessed,
    suspectedRootCauseCategory: parsed.suspectedRootCauseCategory,
    isCriticalProductionOutage: parsed.isCriticalProductionOutage,
    classificationReasoning: parsed.classificationReasoning
  }
}];

