parameters.jsCode:
const upstream = $('JS - Parse Triage Output').first().json;
const runbookResponse = $('HTTP - Search Runbook Knowledge Base').first().json;
const githubIssues = $('GitHub - Search Related Issues & PRs').all().map(i => i.json);
const clickupIncidents = $('ClickUp - Search Previous Incident Tickets').all().map(i => i.json);
const terraformState = $input.first().json;

const runbookMatches = runbookResponse.results || runbookResponse.matches || runbookResponse.documents || [];

return [{
  json: {
    ...upstream,
    retrievedRunbooks: runbookMatches,
    retrievedGithubIssues: githubIssues,
    retrievedPastIncidents: clickupIncidents,
    retrievedTerraformState: terraformState,
    hasRunbookCoverage: runbookMatches.length > 0
  }
}];

parameters.text:
=You are a senior SRE drafting a remediation plan using ONLY the retrieved context below. Do not invent infrastructure details, commands, or history that isn't present in the context.

Service: {{ $json.service }}
Alert type: {{ $json.alertType }}
Severity: {{ $json.severityAssessed }}
Message: {{ $json.alertMessage }}
Suspected root-cause category: {{ $json.suspectedRootCauseCategory }}

Matching runbooks:
{{ JSON.stringify($json.retrievedRunbooks, null, 2) }}

Related GitHub issues/PRs:
{{ JSON.stringify($json.retrievedGithubIssues, null, 2) }}

Previous incident tickets for this service:
{{ JSON.stringify($json.retrievedPastIncidents, null, 2) }}

Current Terraform workspace state:
{{ JSON.stringify($json.retrievedTerraformState, null, 2) }}

Draft a remediation plan:
- rootCauseHypothesis: your best hypothesis, grounded in the context above
- remediationSteps: an ordered array of short, concrete steps a human (or automation) would follow
- actionType: one of 'restart_service', 'scale_out', 'clear_cache', 'rollback_deployment', 'run_terraform_apply', 'other', or 'manual_only' if no safe automated action applies
- autoRemediable: true only if the fix is low-risk, reversible, and fully specified by the runbook/context — false otherwise
- autoRemediationCommand: the specific command/API action to run if autoRemediable is true, otherwise an empty string
- riskLevel: 'Low', 'Medium', or 'High'
- confidence: a number from 0 to 1 reflecting how well the retrieved context supports this plan
- planReasoning: one short sentence explaining the autoRemediable/riskLevel decision

Return ONLY a JSON object (no markdown fences, no commentary) with keys: rootCauseHypothesis, remediationSteps (array of strings), actionType, autoRemediable (boolean), autoRemediationCommand, riskLevel, confidence (number), planReasoning.

parameters.jsCode:
const upstream = $('JS - Aggregate Retrieved Context').first().json;
const response = $input.first().json;

let parsed = {
  rootCauseHypothesis: 'Unable to determine automatically; manual investigation required.',
  remediationSteps: [],
  actionType: 'manual_only',
  autoRemediable: false,
  autoRemediationCommand: '',
  riskLevel: 'High',
  confidence: 0,
  planReasoning: 'AI planning unavailable this cycle; defaulted to manual review as a safety default.'
};
try {
  const raw = String(response.output || response.text || response.response || '{}').replace(/```json|```/g, '').trim();
  const result = JSON.parse(raw);
  parsed = { ...parsed, ...result };
} catch (e) {
  // keep safe default above
}

return [{
  json: {
    ...upstream,
    rootCauseHypothesis: parsed.rootCauseHypothesis,
    remediationSteps: parsed.remediationSteps,
    actionType: parsed.actionType,
    autoRemediable: parsed.autoRemediable,
    autoRemediationCommand: parsed.autoRemediationCommand,
    riskLevel: parsed.riskLevel,
    confidence: parsed.confidence,
    planReasoning: parsed.planReasoning
  }
}];

const item = $input.first().json;
let allowlist = [];
try { allowlist = JSON.parse(item.autoRemediationAllowlistJson || '[]'); } catch (e) { allowlist = []; }

const canAutoRemediate = item.autoRemediable === true
  && item.riskLevel === 'Low'
  && Number(item.confidence) >= 0.75
  && allowlist.includes(item.actionType);

return [{
  json: {
    ...item,
    canAutoRemediate
  }
}];

